#====================================================================
# DRAFT-kea-hook-ping-check-3.0.3-ohos-configure-script-execve
# — OHOS 内核拒 shebang 脚本 execve：Meson 配方 configure 期脚本执行的三层修法
#   与 conan patch-ng 多 hunk 行号语义陷阱（OHOS/kea-hook-ping-check 3.0.3 实测）
# 触发事件: kea-hook-ping-check 3.0.3 适配（真机 conan create 连续四轮递进失败）
# 路径: Path B（知识库扩展）
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-kea-hook-ping-check-3.0.3-ohos-configure-script-execve
trigger_tool:           meson|conan|patch
phase:                  configuration|build
error_signature: "Error 126 while executing|Error 13 while executing|Unhandled python OSError.*Meson|Permission denied.*bin/meson|hunk no.2 doesn't match source file"
root_cause: "The HarmonyOS PC kernel refuses shebang script execve at the syscall level regardless of executable bits (EACCES=Error 13; Error 126 when a subprocess wrapper reports it). Meson-based recipes hit this in three stacked layers: (1) Conan's meson package ships bin/meson as a shell wrapper script, so calling it directly dies before the build starts; (2) the upstream source tree executes its own configure-time helper scripts through meson run_command()/configure_file(command:) — Kea 3.0.3 has five such sites (scripts/env.sh, scripts/grabber.py via GRABBER variable, scripts/cd-and-run.sh, the generated config-report.sh, tools/mk_cfgrpt.sh); (3) some scripts are GENERATED by configure_file() itself, so the exec target is a build-dir artifact, not a source file. A second trap sits in patch application: conan's patch-ng engine interprets each hunk header line number against the source as already patched by PREVIOUS patch FILES (so a patch that adds +6 lines before your hunk shifts its coordinates), while git apply uses pristine-file coordinates — a multi-hunk patch validated with git apply --check can still be rejected by conan with 'hunk no.N doesn't match source file at line X, expected ... actual ...'."
rec_approach: "Layer 1: in build() invoke meson as 'sh <meson pkg>/bin/meson' (sh reads the script without execve; the python3 it spawns is ELF). Layer 2: patch the script VARIABLES, not the call sites — redefine ENV/CD_AND_RUN as ['/bin/sh', <script>] and GRABBER as [find_program('python3').full_path(), <script>], and every run_command keeps passing the variable as first argument; for configure_file(command:) sites patch each command array to ['/bin/sh', <script>, args...]. Sweep the whole tree for remaining direct script execs (grep run_command/command: across every meson.build) including subdir files evaluated AFTER your first crash point. Layer 3 (patch-ng): put multi-hunk patches for the same file in hunk headers whose line numbers are the file state after all EARLIER patch files in conandata (not cumulative over same-file hunks — empirically same-file hunk deltas are not accounted, prior-file deltas are); validate locally with pip-installed patch-ng (fromstring + apply(strip=1)) rather than git apply, which uses different coordinates."
match_keywords: ["shebang execve", "EACCES", "Error 13", "Error 126", "Unhandled python OSError", "meson run_command", "configure_file command", "patch-ng hunk offset", "bin/meson wrapper", "env.sh", "grabber.py", "config-report.sh", "mk_cfgrpt.sh", "interpreter prefix", "HarmonyOS kernel script exec"]
error_excerpt: "meson setup: Running command: scripts/env.sh KEA_PKG_TYPE_IN_CONFIGURE -> ERROR: Unhandled python OSError (conan create Error 13) | Configuring config.report with command -> same | Configuring config_report.cc with command -> same | conan Error 126: /bin/sh: <conan cache>/bin/meson: Permission denied | WARN: 0003-meson.build.patch: hunk no.2 doesn't match source file at line 1022, expected b'CONFIG_REPORT = configure_file(' actual b'config_report_sh = configure_file('"
severity:               2
category:               meson, shell, configure, conan, python, patch, portability, ohos
last_updated: 2026-09-27
